# ── Credentials — NEVER commit these ─────────────────────────────────────────
# A service-account key bypasses every security rule in this repo. Treat a leak
# as a full database compromise: revoke the key in the Google Cloud console
# immediately, do not merely delete the commit.
*service-account*.json
*serviceAccount*.json
sa.json
secrets/
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*

# Google downloads service-account keys as "<project-id>-<key-id>.json" and
# "<project>-firebase-adminsdk-<hash>.json". Neither matches the patterns above,
# so they are named explicitly. A key committed here is a full database
# compromise — the rules in this repo do not apply to the Admin SDK.
expense-manager-204-*.json
*-firebase-adminsdk-*.json
*-[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f].json

# Contains real email addresses of your flatmates.
scripts/member-map.json

# ── Data ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local Firestore exports. These hold everyone's financial history.
backups/

# ── Firebase ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.firebase/
firebase-debug.log*
firestore-debug.log*
ui-debug.log*

# ── Node ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# ── OS / IDE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.code-workspace
